\details{
Conventions reproduced (all times in samples):
\itemize{
\item AF episodes begin at a rhythm annotation whose label starts with \code{"(AFIB"} and end at the next rhythm annotation with any other label. Atrial flutter (\code{"(AFL"}) therefore ends an AF episode.
\item An episode still open at the end of the file ends at the later of the comparison end time and the last annotation read from that file (of any type).
\item The comparison starts at \code{start_time} (default 5 minutes, the \code{epicmp} learning period); episodes of the annotator being scored are clipped to \[\code{start_time}, \code{end_time}\] and the other annotator's episodes are not clipped.
\item The default end is the record length; when the record length is zero or unknown, \code{epicmp} uses \code{end_time = -1}, which selects no episodes. This is reproduced.
